      "text": "Rendezvous How it works Try it Privacy Four routes, one table . Rendezvous lives in iMessage. Text it what you want to do and who's coming. It picks the spot that's fairest to everyone's walk, calls to book the table, tells each of you when to leave, and splits the bill afterward. Plan a dinner here See how it works 7:15 Everyone's at the table Jason North Campus, leaves 6:49 Maya Olin Library, leaves 7:05 Dev Duffield Hall, leaves 7:09 Ana The Commons, leaves 7:00 Sangam table for 4, 7:15 PM Replay",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#how",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 906,
      "width": 1320,
      "height": 4975,
      "heading": "From “dinner?” to “paid back” in one thread",
      "backgroundColor": "#EEF1F4",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "From “dinner?” to “paid back” in one thread Ask Say what you want and who's coming Text Rendezvous like you'd text a friend. It saves everyone's numbers, so next time \"dinner with the roommates\" is enough. No app to download. It's just iMessage. Plan It finds the fairest spot It checks when everyone's free, what they can spend, and how far each person walks. Then it picks the place where the longest walk is shortest. Calendars share free/busy only. Balances and locations stay private. Agree Everyone taps 👍, or asks for a change A reply like “can we do Indian instead” starts a new round in sec",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#try",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 5977,
      "width": 1920,
      "height": 1345,
      "heading": "Now plan one yourself",
      "backgroundColor": "#0E1B2C",
      "callsToAction": [
        "@Rendezvous dinner tonight, under $15 each",
        "@Rendezvous lunch tomorrow at noon",
        "Ask",
        "Plan",
        "Agree",
        "Book",
        "Go",
        "Settle"
      ],
      "text": "Now plan one yourself This runs the real Rendezvous planner in your browser. You're Jason, with three pretend friends, a pretend restaurant and pretend money. Type anything, or tap a suggestion. 5:41 M D A Dinner crew Maya, Dev, Ana and Rendezvous Today 5:41 PM You're Jason, and Maya, Dev and Ana are in this chat with Rendezvous. Mention it below and say what you want to do. @Rendezvous dinner tonight, under $15 each @Rendezvous lunch tomorrow at noon Message the group as Jason Ask Plan Agree Book Go Settle Someone texts Rendezvous what they want to do and who's coming, or mentions it in a gro",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#privacy",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 7323,
      "width": 1320,
      "height": 832,
      "heading": "It knows just enough",
      "backgroundColor": "#EEF1F4",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "It knows just enough Rendezvous takes the least it needs for each step, and nothing moves without the right person's say-so. Calendars It sees when you're busy, never what you're doing. Event names and guests stay on your calendar. Location Where you are only feeds the walking math. Nobody else in the plan sees it. Balances Your balance only rules out places you can't afford. Nobody in the chat ever sees it. Payments Money moves only when the person who owes taps 👍 on their own line. Anyone else's tap is ignored. Phone calls It says it's an AI at the start of every call, and it never speaks o",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    },
    {
      "selector": "#built",
      "type": "content",
      "x": 300,
      "y": 8154,
      "width": 1320,
      "height": 568,
      "heading": "What it runs on",
      "backgroundColor": "#EEF1F4",
      "callsToAction": [],
      "text": "What it runs on One agent server holds the plan and talks to the group through Photon. A separate Python bridge handles the phone audio. Built in Cursor at BigRed//Hacks 2026. Photon The whole interface: iMessage threads and group chats, tapback approvals and departure texts. Grok Reads what the group asks for, and Grok Voice places the reservation call. Capital One Nessie Ithaca restaurants as merchants, budgets from balances, and the transfers that settle the bill. Google Maps and Calendar Walking times for every route, and free/busy for every calendar. Twilio and Pipecat Bridge the restaura",
      "layout": "centered",
      "assetUrls": []
    }
  ],
